<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Agent loop.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One loop is shared by all arms (<a href="#S3.F1" title="In 3 Study design ‣ Good Judgment, Bad Advice: Decision-Model ControllersRaise Agent Cost Without Improving Success" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
Each step is one call to the reasoning model, which may invoke <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bash</span> or <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">finish</span>; a reply without a tool call counts as a finish request.
Commands run through Harbor <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Harbor contributors, 2026</a>)</cite> in a fresh shell inside a Daytona sandbox <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Daytona, 2026</a>)</cite> built from the task’s own image.
Tool output is truncated to its first 4,000 and last 8,000 characters, the context is never compacted, and the loop and all API keys stay on the host.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Decision points.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Four deterministic triggers are detected in every arm, including the one without a controller, and the state at each is logged:
T1, repeated failure (two or more consecutive failing commands);
T2, no progress (a repeated command or repeated output);
T3, a finish request;
T4, a checkpoint every 10 steps.
At most one trigger fires per step, and a trigger type cannot refire within three steps (exact definitions in <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Parameters ‣ Good Judgment, Bad Advice: Decision-Model ControllersRaise Agent Cost Without Improving Success" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Questions and actions.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At T1, T2 and T4 the controller answers <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Q-progress</em> with <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">continue</span>, <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">investigate</span>, <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">recover</span> or <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">abandon</span>; at T3 it answers <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Q-finish</em> with <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">finish</span> or <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">verify</span>.
<span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">investigate</span>, <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">recover</span> and <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">verify</span> append one of three fixed advisory messages (<a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Prompts and messages ‣ Good Judgment, Bad Advice: Decision-Model ControllersRaise Agent Cost Without Improving Success" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>) that never contain commands, paths or test information; <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">abandon</span> ends the run as a failure and <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">finish</span> ends it normally.
The controller sees only a compact state built from the agent’s transcript: the instruction, the trigger, step and spend against their caps, the last five commands with exit codes and output tails, failure and repetition counters, whether a verification-like command ran after the last edit, the finish summary, and its own earlier choices.
It never sees tests, verifier output or reference solutions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Controllers.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Native</em> detects and logs triggers but never consults a controller.
<em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Rules</em> answers <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">recover</span> at T1 and T2, <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">continue</span> at T4, <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">verify</span> at T3 unless a verification-like command ran after the last edit, and <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">abandon</span> after four consecutive failures once 40% of the step budget is used.
The <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">small LLM</em> is Claude Haiku 5.5 with reasoning disabled; it receives the same state and option descriptions as Jev and must return a single choice under a JSON schema.
<em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Jev</em> is <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">typesafe/jev-1.13</span> (served snapshot <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jev-1.13-20260917</span>) asked a <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.11" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">choice</em> question with the same descriptions.
The <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.12" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">placebo</em> samples from Jev’s development-phase frequencies (Q-progress: continue 0.625, investigate 0.125, recover 0.25, abandon 0; Q-finish: finish 0.652, verify 0.348), seeded per trial.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Guards.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Guards override every controller.
G1 enforces hard limits on steps, spend, tokens and wall time.
G2 allows <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">abandon</span> only once 40% of the step budget is used and the run shows a failure streak or repeated lack of progress; otherwise it becomes <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">recover</span>.
G3 accepts the third finish request after two <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">verify</span> answers.
G4 replaces a timeout, transport error or malformed answer with <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">continue</span> or <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">finish</span>, and logs it.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Models and infrastructure.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All models are called through OpenRouter <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenRouter, 2026</a>)</cite>.
Sonnet 5.5 runs with reasoning effort <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">high</em> (reasoning is mandatory for this model) and prompt caching; no Sonnet 5.5 endpoint accepts a temperature parameter, so sampling is not greedy.
Hosts are chosen by OpenRouter among endpoints that support every request parameter; of 4,780 main-model calls in the evaluation, 94.6% were served by Claude Platform on AWS and 5.4% by Azure, with a similar mix in every arm.
Cost is the provider-reported cost of every reasoning-model and controller call; sandbox compute is excluded.
Harbor 0.24.0 runs the task’s verifier after the agent stops and enforces each task’s own agent timeout (at most 60 minutes for the tasks used); a reward of 1 is a pass.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Protocol.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Terminal-Bench 2.1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Terminal-Bench contributors, 2026</a>)</cite> has 89 tasks; we pinned the hub dataset by content digest and excluded two tasks whose agent timeouts exceed 60 minutes and one that Sonnet 5.5 refuses on its first turn (found during calibration, before the split).
<em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Calibration:</em> 30 tasks sampled across categories were run twice with native under generous caps (100 steps, $3), stratified as <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hard</em> (0/2 passes), <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mid</em> (1/2) or <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">easy</em> (2/2), and split into 8 development tasks (6 easy, 1 mid, 1 hard) and 21 held-out tasks (14 easy, 3 mid, 4 hard); calibration attempts are not used in any result.
<em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Caps</em> were set to 60 steps and $1.00 per trial for every arm, above every calibration run (passing runs: at most 52 steps and $0.48; all runs: at most $0.98).
<em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Development:</em> the four non-placebo arms ran twice on the development tasks; nothing was tuned, and the runs only supplied the placebo distribution.
<em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Evaluation:</em> with the held-out list checksummed and every configuration fingerprinted, 21 tasks <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 5 arms <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 3 attempts gave 315 trials, with arm order randomized within each task–attempt block.
No trial failed for infrastructure reasons; model spend was $59.46 for the evaluation and $72.29 in total.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Statistics.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each task and arm we average over attempts and compare arms paired by task, resampling tasks 10,000 times <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Efron and Tibshirani, 1993</a>)</cite> for percentile 95% intervals.
The cost effect is the geometric mean over tasks of the per-task ratio of USD per attempt.
The confirmatory comparison C1 (Jev vs. native) tests the cost ratio and checks the pass-rate difference against a pre-specified margin of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-10</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points (pp) using the one-sided 95% lower bound.
C2–C4 compare Jev with the small LLM, rules and placebo, with Holm-adjusted bootstrap <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Holm, 1979</a>)</cite>.
<a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Offline decision quality ‣ 4 Results ‣ Good Judgment, Bad Advice: Decision-Model ControllersRaise Agent Cost Without Improving Success" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sections</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> and <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Where the extra cost comes from ‣ 4 Results ‣ Good Judgment, Bad Advice: Decision-Model ControllersRaise Agent Cost Without Improving Success" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> are exploratory.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
