<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Confirmatory: Jev versus no controller</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Jev increased cost per attempt by 19% (geometric-mean ratio 1.19, 95% CI 1.02–1.36; <a href="#S4.T2" title="In 4 Results ‣ Good Judgment, Bad Advice: Decision-Model ControllersRaise Agent Cost Without Improving Success" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
The pass rate was identical, 73.0% in both arms (difference <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.0</annotation></semantics></math> pp, 95% CI <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-11.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>11.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-11.1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+12.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>12.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+12.7</annotation></semantics></math>).
The one-sided 95% lower bound, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-9.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-9.5</annotation></semantics></math> pp, lies just inside the <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-10</annotation></semantics></math> pp margin; with 21 tasks this is at the limit of what the design can resolve, so we read it as no evidence of a large drop rather than as noninferiority.
The hypothesis that Jev lowers cost is rejected.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Secondary: small LLM, rules and placebo</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Jev cost 19% less than the small LLM making the same decisions and 22% more than the placebo, and matched the rules arm; no pass-rate difference was detectable (<a href="#S4.T2" title="In 4 Results ‣ Good Judgment, Bad Advice: Decision-Model ControllersRaise Agent Cost Without Improving Success" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
Against native (<a href="#S4.F2.sf1" title="In Figure 2 ‣ 4.2 Secondary: small LLM, rules and placebo ‣ 4 Results ‣ Good Judgment, Bad Advice: Decision-Model ControllersRaise Agent Cost Without Improving Success" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(a)</span></a>), all three informed controllers raised cost (rules <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>1.24, 95% CI 1.12–1.38; small LLM <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>1.47, 1.16–1.86; Jev <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>1.19), whereas the placebo did not (<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>0.98, 0.78–1.16).</p>
</div>
